[Music]  if only the air quality were better in  london rossamond kissy deborah's  daughter might still be alive today  [Music]  ella was almost seven when she suddenly  became very ill  my late daughter is ella roberta and she  had one of the worst cases of asthma  ever recorded in this country so it  started in october you know signs of a  cold a cough that sounded like whooping  cough and her first admission or her  first  coma or seizure was in december it was  linked to air pollution  and through my research i found out that  air pollution it affects millions  worldwide  until she fell ill ella was a completely  healthy child and very sporty she loved  swimming and football and also played  several instruments the asthma changed  everything  my life was rushing to work and then  always having my phone near me in case  her school rang to say her lungs had  collapsed  ella suffered for two years before dying  of an asthma attack her mother became an  activist  with the help of doctors and liars she  was able to prove that her daughter's  asthma was particularly bad on days when  the air pollution was extremely high  i wanted it officially recognized i  thought for all she suffered she  deserved that 28 months of her  suffocating in her mucus basically  she deserved to have that moment  i don't want other children in this  country to go through  what my late daughter went through  london has a problem most of the city  exceeds the world health organization's  air pollution limits many of the famous  black cabs run on diesel which is  particularly bad for air quality  hundreds of londoners end up in the  emergency room each year because of  toxic air the mayor sadiq khan has  introduced countermeasures and stiff  charges for drivers with older more  polluting cars but it's not enough  we've shown the way with some  world-leading policies from the world's  first ultra-emission zone to reckon  number of electric buses increasing  hugely the number of charging points 